      {
        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 10,
        "titulo": "Reflexive verbs: the small pronoun is not optional",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: a reflexive verb is one where the action comes back to the person doing it. In the dictionary it ends in «-si»: «alzarsi», «lavarsi», «vestirsi». STEP 2: English often leaves the pronoun out: «I wash», «I get up», «I get dressed». Italian keeps it: «mi lavo», «mi alzo», «mi vesto». STEP 3: take off «-si», conjugate the verb as usual and put the pronoun in front: «mi alzo, ti alzi, si alza, ci alziamo, vi alzate, si alzano». STEP 4: the pronouns are «mi, ti, si, ci, vi, si». STEP 5: the negation goes before the pronoun: «Non mi sveglio mai presto». STEP 6: questions keep the pronoun before the verb, with no helper word: «A che ora ti alzi?». STEP 7: with body parts and clothes, Italian uses the article, not «my»: «Mi lavo le mani» (I wash my hands). The pronoun «mi» already shows whose hands they are. STEP 8: some verbs are reflexive in Italian but not in English: «svegliarsi» (to wake up), «addormentarsi» (to fall asleep), «divertirsi» (to have fun). STEP 9: after «volere», «potere», «dovere» and «sapere», the pronoun can go before the modal or attach to the infinitive: «Mi devo alzare presto» or «Devo alzarmi presto».",
        "comparacao": "English hides the reflexive: «I get up» does not say «myself». Italian says it every time: «mi alzo», literally «I raise myself». The «my» of body parts is the other loss: English says «I wash my hands», but Italian says «mi lavo le mani», and nobody adds «mie». The listening trap is the little word «mi»: without it, the sentence can change meaning, as «lavo le mani» would sound like «I wash the hands (of someone else)».",
        "exemplos": [
          {
            "ru": "Mi alzo alle sette",
            "pt": "I get up at seven"
          },
          {
            "ru": "Mi lavo le mani",
            "pt": "I wash my hands"
          },
          {
            "ru": "Si divertono molto",
            "pt": "They have a lot of fun"
          },
          {
            "ru": "Non mi sveglio mai presto",
            "pt": "I never wake up early"
          }
        ],
